# bloomery reference sets

The oracle files of the fixture tier of [bloomery](https://github.com/midagedev/bloomery): intermediate tensors
that ik_llama.cpp dumped while it ran bloomery's fixture models. A fixture is a GGUF with random weights and the
shape of a real model. The sets are raw little-endian f32 tensors plus a `MANIFEST.tsv` each. They hold no model
weights. bloomery's gates compare the engine against them.

Sets: @SET_COUNT@. Files: @FILE_COUNT@. Size: @TOTAL_GB@ GB.

@FAMILY_TABLE@

## Make the fixture files

The sets belong to fixtures, and the fixtures are not in this repo. `fixture fetch` makes one
from the headers of its source model's files (a few MB per shard); its table of sources is in the bloomery repo
(`crates/model/src/bin/fixture.rs`, `SPECS`):

```
@FETCH_COMMANDS@
```

The DeepSeek V4.1 DSpark draft fixture cannot be fetched, so no set of it is here. The set
`ref-mtp/fx_qwen4exp_prose64_n64_k1` also names the fixture's MTP draft file,
`/models/fixtures/qwen38/mtp-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-shared-Q8_0.gguf`, which `fixture fetch` makes with the fixture.

## The path is part of the identity

A set states the fixture it was dumped from by its full path, `/models/fixtures/<dir>/<file>`. Make the fixtures at
those paths. On a machine without `/models`, make `/models/fixtures` a symlink to where you keep them.

## Put the sets in place

The repo mirrors `$BLOOMERY_DATA`: a set is `fx_.../<file>` or `ref-mtp/fx_.../<file>`, the path the gates read. One
download is the whole install:

```
hf download --repo-type dataset @REPO@ --local-dir "$BLOOMERY_DATA"
```

To take one family, name its sets with `--include`. The sets of each family:

@SET_LIST@

Optional check, from `$BLOOMERY_DATA`: `sha256sum --quiet -c SHA256SUMS`. It lists every file of the repo, so on a
partial download it reports the files you did not take as missing. The download also puts `README.md` and
`SHA256SUMS` in `$BLOOMERY_DATA`.

